{number: 163}
{title: Sun of My Soul}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[F] Sun of my soul, Thou [Bb] Savior [F] dear,
It is not night if [C7] Thou be [F] near;
O may no earthborn [Bb] cloud a-[F] rise
To hide Thee from Thy [C7] servant's [F] eyes.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
When [F] the soft dews of [Bb] kindly [F] sleep
My wearied eyelids [C7] gently [F] steep,
Be my last thought, how [Bb] sweet to [F] rest
Forever on my [C7] Savior's [F] breast.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
A-[F] bide with me from [Bb] morn till [F] eve,
For without Thee I [C7] cannot [F] live;
Abide with me when [Bb] night is [F] nigh,
For without Thee I [C7] dare not [F] die.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Come [F] near and bless us [Bb] when we [F] wake,
Ere through the world our [C7] way we [F] take,
Till in the ocean [Bb] of Thy [F] love
We lose ourselves in [C7] heaven a-[F] bove.
{end_of_verse}
